Built something meaningful today.

After a long stretch of debugging, rewrites, dead ends, and persistence, I brought Project Ocean to life in a real way:

A private local AI system that can:
• hold conversation
• understand intent
• store memory
• preserve context between sessions
• evolve without relying on the cloud

This matters to me because I believe the future of AI should be more personal, more private, and more aligned with the human using it.

Not just smarter tools. Real collaboration.

Today wasn’t glamorous. It was terminal windows, syntax errors, path bugs, and stubborn determination.

But that’s what building actually looks like.

We’re still early. More to come.

